# Entity Model (Persistence Only)

Entities are **not** API contracts. No Jakarta validation on entities used at the API boundary.

## Required patterns

- `@Table("snake_case_table")` from `org.springframework.data.relational.core.mapping.Table`
- `@Id` from `org.springframework.data.annotation.Id`
- No-arg constructor with comment: `// Required by Spring Data JDBC for object materialization.`
- Manual getters/setters (no Lombok)
- `@Nullable` on optional fields; `@Nullable LocalDateTime createdAt` when column exists

## FK relationships

Use `AggregateReference<RelatedEntity, Long>` — not plain `Long` on entities:

```java
private AggregateReference<Event, Long> eventId;
```

Convert from DTO `Long` ids in mapper/service when saving.

## Do not

- Add `@NotBlank` / `@Valid` to entities exposed via REST (put validation on request DTOs)
- Return entities directly from controllers
- Use JPA annotations (`@Entity`, `@Column`) — this project uses Spring Data JDBC
